---
import PartnerOffers from "../components/PartnerOffers.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import routePages from "../../data/route-pages.json";
import benchmarkData from "../../data/coefficients.json";
import { formatReviewDate, marginSummary, trustSources } from "../lib/trust.js";

const routeSlugs = routePages.routes.map(route => route.slug);
const reviewDate = formatReviewDate(benchmarkData.last_reviewed);
const uhaulPeriod = benchmarkData.sources.uhaul.data_period;
const margin = marginSummary();
const methodologyUrl = new URL("/methodology/", Astro.site).href;
const trustList = trustSources(benchmarkData.sources);

const pageUrl = new URL("/calculator/", Astro.site).href;
const appJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebApplication",
  name: "Relocation Cost moving budget calculator",
  url: pageUrl,
  applicationCategory: "FinanceApplication",
  operatingSystem: "Any",
  browserRequirements: "Requires JavaScript",
  description: "Free planning calculator for US state-to-state moves. Combines distance, home size, move type and other relocation costs into a budget range. Estimates are planning aids, not quotes.",
  offers: { "@type": "Offer", price: "0", priceCurrency: "USD" }
};
const breadcrumbJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  itemListElement: [
    { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: new URL("/", Astro.site).href },
    { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Calculator", item: pageUrl }
  ]
};
---
<Layout title="Moving Cost Calculator — Relocation Cost" description="Build a relocation budget from move distance, home size, move type, and additional relocation costs. Free planning estimate for any US state-to-state move.">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(appJsonLd)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbJsonLd)} />
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14 pb-28 lg:pb-14">
    <div class="max-w-3xl print:hidden">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-700">Relocation Cost Suite</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Build your moving budget</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">Start with a transport planning estimate, then add the costs that can make a relocation more expensive than the move itself.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1.15fr_.85fr] print:hidden">
      <form id="calculator" class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8" novalidate>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Move details</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">From State
            <select id="fromState" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" aria-describedby="stateHelp"></select>
          </label>
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">To State
            <select id="toState" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" aria-describedby="stateHelp"></select>
          </label>
        </div>
        <p id="stateHelp" class="mt-2 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">The distance is filled in as an approximate straight line between the centers of the two states. It is not road mileage. If you know your actual driving miles, type them in below to replace it.</p>

        <div class="mt-5 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Distance <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(miles)</span>
            <input id="distance" type="number" min="1" max="30000" value="1317" inputmode="numeric" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3 outline-none focus:border-sky-500" />
          </label>
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Home size
            <select id="size" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3">
              <option value="1">Studio / 1 room</option><option value="1.35">2–3 rooms</option><option value="1.8">4–5 rooms</option><option value="2.4">6+ rooms</option>
            </select>
          </label>
        </div>
        <label class="mt-5 block text-sm font-semibold">Move type
          <select id="type" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3">
            <option value="0.65">DIY</option><option value="1">Rental truck + labor</option><option value="1.65">Full-service movers</option>
          </select>
        </label>

        <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold">Other relocation costs</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Enter amounts you already know. Anything left at $0 is left out of the total. It does not mean that cost is free, so add it once you know it.</p>
        <div class="mt-5 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Travel <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(USD)</span><input id="travel" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Temporary housing <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(USD)</span><input id="housing" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Deposits / setup <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(USD)</span><input id="setup" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Packing / extras <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(USD)</span><input id="extras" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
        </div>
        <h3 class="mt-8 text-base font-bold">Itemize your costs <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(optional)</span></h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Add known amounts one by one. They are added on top of the fields above, so do not enter the same cost twice. Left at $0, an item is left out of the total. It does not mean that cost is free.</p>
        <div class="mt-5 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Fuel <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(USD)</span><input id="fuel" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Moving insurance <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(USD)</span><input id="insurance" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Packing materials <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(USD)</span><input id="packing" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Equipment rental <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(dolly, ramp, USD)</span><input id="equipment" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Utility connection fees <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(USD)</span><input id="utilities" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Storage <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(USD)</span><input id="storage" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Crew tips <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(USD)</span><input id="tips" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Specialty items <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(piano, safe, hot tub, USD)</span><input id="specialty" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold sm:col-span-2">Access fees <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(stairs, long carry, elevator, USD)</span><input id="access" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
        </div>

        <h3 class="mt-8 text-base font-bold">Employer relocation package <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(optional)</span></h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">If your employer offers help, enter it to see how much of your estimate it covers. Enter amounts as you will receive or use them. Lump sums can be taxed, so ask your employer whether the amount is before or after tax. This calculator does not work out taxes.</p>
        <div class="mt-5 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Lump sum paid to you <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(USD)</span><input id="employerCash" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Costs the employer pays directly <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(movers, housing, USD)</span><input id="employerDirect" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
        </div>

        <h3 class="mt-8 text-base font-bold">Cash buffer until your first income <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(optional)</span></h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Money to keep available for living costs until you are paid at the new place. It is shown separately, because it is cash you hold rather than an estimated moving expense.</p>
        <div class="mt-5 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Weeks to cover
            <select id="reserveWeeks" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3">
              <option value="0">None</option><option value="2">2 weeks</option><option value="4">4 weeks</option><option value="6">6 weeks</option><option value="8">8 weeks</option><option value="12">12 weeks</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Living costs per week <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(USD)</span><input id="weeklyLiving" type="number" min="0" max="100000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
        </div>
        <p id="inputError" class="mt-4 min-h-5 text-sm font-medium text-red-700" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-slate-500">The estimate updates as you type.</p>
        <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <button id="share" class="rounded-xl bg-slate-950 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-slate-800" type="button">Share this estimate</button>
          <button id="reset" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-900 hover:bg-slate-50" type="button">Reset calculator</button>
        </div>
        <button id="print" class="mt-3 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-900 hover:bg-slate-50" type="button">Print or save as PDF</button>
        <p id="shareStatus" class="mt-3 min-h-5 break-all text-sm text-slate-500" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">This calculator covers the planning inputs shown above. It does not automatically include taxes, insurance, utility connection fees, or real-estate costs unless you enter them under “Other relocation costs”. See the <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href="/methodology/">methodology</a> for how the estimate is built.</p>
      </form>

      <aside class="h-fit rounded-2xl bg-slate-950 p-7 text-white sm:p-8 lg:sticky lg:top-6">
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">Estimated relocation budget</p>
        <div id="result" class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold">$0</div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-300">Planning estimate, not a quote. Replace assumptions with provider quotes as you get them.</p>
        <div class="mt-7 space-y-3 border-t border-slate-800 pt-5 text-sm">
          <div class="flex justify-between"><span class="text-slate-400">Move</span><strong id="moveResult">$0</strong></div>
          <div class="flex justify-between"><span class="text-slate-400">Other costs</span><strong id="otherResult">$0</strong></div>
          <div class="flex justify-between"><span class="text-slate-400">Contingency (10%)</span><strong id="contingencyResult">$0</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-6 border-t border-slate-800 pt-5 text-sm text-slate-400">Indicative range <strong id="range" class="text-white">$0–$0</strong></div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">Margin of error: a fixed {margin.label} planning band, not a statistical interval. Benchmark data reviewed {reviewDate}. <a class="font-semibold text-sky-300 underline" href="#trust-heading">Sources</a></p>
        <div id="cashBox" class="mt-5 space-y-2 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900 p-4 text-sm" hidden>
          <div class="flex justify-between"><span class="text-slate-400">Cash buffer</span><strong id="reserveResult">$0</strong></div>
          <div class="flex justify-between border-t border-slate-800 pt-2"><span class="text-slate-300">Cash to have ready</span><strong id="cashNeededResult">$0</strong></div>
          <p class="text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">Budget plus your cash buffer. The buffer is outside the contingency and the indicative range.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="employerBox" class="mt-5 space-y-2 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900 p-4 text-sm" hidden>
          <p class="font-semibold text-slate-200">Employer package</p>
          <div class="flex justify-between"><span class="text-slate-400">Covered by your employer</span><strong id="employerCovered">$0</strong></div>
          <div class="flex justify-between border-t border-slate-800 pt-2"><span id="employerGapLabel" class="text-slate-300">Gap you would pay</span><strong id="employerGapValue">$0</strong></div>
          <p id="employerGapRange" class="text-xs leading-5 text-slate-400"></p>
          <p id="employerBufferRow" class="text-xs leading-5 text-slate-400" hidden>Including your cash buffer: <strong id="employerBufferGap" class="text-slate-200"></strong></p>
          <p class="text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">Estimated budget minus what the employer covers. It is not a tax calculation, and a planning estimate is not a quote.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900 p-4 text-sm">
          <p class="font-semibold text-slate-200">Published truck-rental average</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-slate-400">U-Haul published one-way rental average for this mileage band: <strong id="marketBenchmark" class="text-white">$0</strong>.</p>
          <p id="floorNote" class="mt-2 text-xs leading-5 text-sky-300" hidden>The move cost starts from this average because the basic model came out lower.</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">It is used only as a minimum in the DIY base for the move cost. It is an average for the whole mileage band, not a quote for your route.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="nextSteps" class="mt-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900 p-4 text-sm" data-route-slugs={JSON.stringify(routeSlugs)}>
          <p class="font-semibold text-slate-200">Next steps</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
            <li id="routeGuideItem" hidden><a id="routeGuideLink" href="/moving-cost/" class="font-semibold text-sky-300 underline">Route guide</a></li>
            <li><a href="/guides/diy-vs-movers/" class="font-semibold text-sky-300 underline">DIY vs movers</a>: when each option usually makes sense</li>
            <li><a href="/guides/reading-a-moving-quote/" class="font-semibold text-sky-300 underline">Reading a moving quote</a>: binding vs non-binding estimates</li>
            <li><a href="/guides/relocation-budget/" class="font-semibold text-sky-300 underline">Relocation budget guide</a>: costs beyond the move itself</li>
            <li><a href="/checklist/" class="font-semibold text-sky-300 underline">Moving checklist</a>: what to do and when</li>
            <li><a href="/budget-tracker/" class="font-semibold text-sky-300 underline">Budget tracker</a>: planned vs what you actually spend</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <section id="printSummary" class="hidden print:block" aria-label="Printable budget summary">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-700">Relocation Cost</p>
      <h2 class="mt-1 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Relocation budget summary</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">Prepared <span id="printDate"></span> at relocation-cost-psi.vercel.app/calculator/</p>
      <dl class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Route</dt><dd id="printRoute" class="text-slate-700"></dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Distance</dt><dd id="printDistance" class="text-slate-700"></dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Home size</dt><dd id="printSize" class="text-slate-700"></dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Move type</dt><dd id="printType" class="text-slate-700"></dd></div>
      </dl>
      <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-bold">Costs you entered</h3>
      <ul id="printCosts" class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm"></ul>
      <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-bold">Estimate</h3>
      <dl class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm">
        <div class="flex justify-between"><dt class="text-slate-700">Move</dt><dd id="printMove" class="font-semibold"></dd></div>
        <div class="flex justify-between"><dt class="text-slate-700">Other costs</dt><dd id="printOther" class="font-semibold"></dd></div>
        <div class="flex justify-between"><dt class="text-slate-700">Contingency (10%)</dt><dd id="printContingency" class="font-semibold"></dd></div>
        <div class="flex justify-between border-t border-slate-300 pt-1 text-base"><dt class="font-bold">Estimated budget</dt><dd id="printTotal" class="font-bold"></dd></div>
        <div class="flex justify-between"><dt class="text-slate-700">Indicative range</dt><dd id="printRange" class="font-semibold"></dd></div>
        <div id="printEmployerRow" class="flex justify-between" hidden><dt class="text-slate-700">Covered by your employer</dt><dd id="printEmployer" class="font-semibold"></dd></div>
        <div id="printEmployerGapRow" class="flex justify-between" hidden><dt class="font-bold">Employer gap</dt><dd id="printEmployerGap" class="font-bold"></dd></div>
        <div id="printReserveRow" class="flex justify-between" hidden><dt class="text-slate-700">Cash buffer</dt><dd id="printReserve" class="font-semibold"></dd></div>
        <div id="printCashRow" class="flex justify-between" hidden><dt class="font-bold">Cash to have ready</dt><dd id="printCash" class="font-bold"></dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-600">Planning estimate, not a quote. Distance is a straight line between state centers unless you entered your own miles. Costs left at $0 are left out of the total. Replace these assumptions with route-specific provider quotes.</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-600">Range is a fixed {margin.label} planning band. Benchmark data reviewed {reviewDate}; U-Haul figures from {uhaulPeriod}. Sources: {methodologyUrl}</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8" aria-labelledby="breakdown-heading">
      <h2 id="breakdown-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Where your budget goes</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Each part of the estimated budget as a share of the total. The cash buffer is not included, because it is cash you hold rather than an estimated expense.</p>
      <div id="breakdownBar" class="mt-5 flex h-5 w-full overflow-hidden rounded-full bg-slate-100" role="img" aria-label="Cost breakdown is not available yet"></div>
      <ul id="breakdownList" class="mt-5 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-3 text-sm sm:grid-cols-2"></ul>
      <p id="breakdownNote" class="mt-3 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">Shares are rounded to whole percentages that add up to 100%.</p>
      <h3 class="mt-8 text-lg font-bold">Ways to keep the budget down</h3>
      <ul id="tipsList" class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700"></ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8 print:hidden" aria-labelledby="missed-heading">
      <h2 id="missed-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Costs people often forget</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">None of these are guessed for you. Ask each provider whether it applies, then enter the amount in the matching field above.</p>
      <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600 md:grid-cols-2">
        <li><strong class="text-slate-900">Stairs, long carries and elevators.</strong> Some movers charge extra when access is difficult. Field: Access fees.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-slate-900">Heavy or fragile items.</strong> Pianos, safes and hot tubs are often quoted separately. Field: Specialty items.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-slate-900">Crew tips.</strong> Not usually part of a quote. Field: Crew tips.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-slate-900">Storage between homes.</strong> A gap between leases or closings can mean paying for storage. Field: Storage.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-slate-900">Fuel and tolls.</strong> Easy to miss with a rental truck. Field: Fuel.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-slate-900">Coverage.</strong> Check what the mover or rental company already includes. Field: Moving insurance.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8 print:hidden" aria-labelledby="read-heading">
      <h2 id="read-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">How to read your estimate</h2>
      <dl class="mt-5 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-4 text-sm leading-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Move</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">The modelled cost of transporting your move. It comes from the distance, home size and move type, and it is a planning assumption.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Other costs</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">Only the amounts you typed in, including any itemized costs. A cost left at $0 is not in the total. It is not known to be free.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Cash buffer and cash to have ready</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">Weeks to cover times your weekly living costs. It is cash you plan to hold until your first income, so it is added after the estimate and is not part of the contingency or the range.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Contingency (10%)</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">A 10% planning buffer added on top of the move and your other costs.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Indicative range</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">The total minus 20% to the total plus 20%. It is a planning range, not a quote and not a statistically validated confidence interval.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Published truck-rental average</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">U-Haul's published average one-way truck rental for your mileage band. The DIY base never goes below it. It is not your actual quote.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Distance</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">Filled in as a straight line between state centers, not road mileage. Replace it with your driving miles when you know them.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">Each amount is rounded to the nearest dollar for display, so the parts can differ from the total by a dollar.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8 print:hidden" aria-labelledby="trust-heading">
      <h2 id="trust-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">How reliable is this estimate?</h2>
      <dl class="mt-5 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-4 text-sm leading-6 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div>
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Last updated</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">Benchmark data reviewed on {reviewDate}. The U-Haul figures describe {uhaulPeriod}.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Margin of error</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">The indicative range is the total {margin.label}. It is a fixed planning band. It has not been checked against real quotes, so your actual price can fall outside it.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">What is assumed</dt>
          <dd class="text-slate-600">The base amount, per-mile rate, home-size and move-type multipliers and the {margin.contingency}% contingency are planning assumptions, not market prices.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600"><strong class="text-slate-900">Independence:</strong> the formula is the same whether or not a provider pays us. Affiliate links, if any, never change an estimate. See the <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a>.</p>
      <h3 class="mt-6 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900">Sources</h3>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
        {trustList.map(source => (
          <li><a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href={source.url} rel="noopener">{source.name}</a>. {source.role}.</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">Full formula and known limits: <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href="/methodology/">methodology</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 print:hidden" aria-labelledby="compare-heading">
      <h2 id="compare-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Compare move types</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Same distance, home size and other costs as above, with each move type. Planning estimates, not quotes.</p>
      <div class="mt-5 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <div data-compare-type="0.65" data-selected="false" class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm data-[selected=true]:border-sky-500 data-[selected=true]:ring-2 data-[selected=true]:ring-sky-200">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-500">DIY</p>
          <p data-compare-total class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">$0</p>
          <p data-compare-range class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500">$0–$0</p>
        </div>
        <div data-compare-type="1" data-selected="false" class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm data-[selected=true]:border-sky-500 data-[selected=true]:ring-2 data-[selected=true]:ring-sky-200">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-500">Rental truck + labor</p>
          <p data-compare-total class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">$0</p>
          <p data-compare-range class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500">$0–$0</p>
        </div>
        <div data-compare-type="1.65" data-selected="false" class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm data-[selected=true]:border-sky-500 data-[selected=true]:ring-2 data-[selected=true]:ring-sky-200">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-500">Full-service movers</p>
          <p data-compare-total class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">$0</p>
          <p data-compare-range class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500">$0–$0</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 print:hidden" aria-labelledby="compare-size-heading">
      <h2 id="compare-size-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Compare home sizes</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Same distance, move type and other costs as above, with each home size. Planning estimates, not quotes.</p>
      <div class="mt-5 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        <div data-compare-size="1" data-selected="false" class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm data-[selected=true]:border-sky-500 data-[selected=true]:ring-2 data-[selected=true]:ring-sky-200">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-500">Studio / 1 room</p>
          <p data-compare-total class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">$0</p>
          <p data-compare-range class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500">$0–$0</p>
        </div>
        <div data-compare-size="1.35" data-selected="false" class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm data-[selected=true]:border-sky-500 data-[selected=true]:ring-2 data-[selected=true]:ring-sky-200">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-500">2–3 rooms</p>
          <p data-compare-total class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">$0</p>
          <p data-compare-range class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500">$0–$0</p>
        </div>
        <div data-compare-size="1.8" data-selected="false" class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm data-[selected=true]:border-sky-500 data-[selected=true]:ring-2 data-[selected=true]:ring-sky-200">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-500">4–5 rooms</p>
          <p data-compare-total class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">$0</p>
          <p data-compare-range class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500">$0–$0</p>
        </div>
        <div data-compare-size="2.4" data-selected="false" class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm data-[selected=true]:border-sky-500 data-[selected=true]:ring-2 data-[selected=true]:ring-sky-200">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-500">6+ rooms</p>
          <p data-compare-total class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">$0</p>
          <p data-compare-range class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500">$0–$0</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">With DIY, the published U-Haul average for the distance band often sets the minimum move cost, so several home sizes can show the same total. That is a rule of this model. It does not mean a larger home costs the same, because the model has no separate truck-size price. Rental truck + labor and full-service add a home-size premium, so those totals differ by size. See the <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href="/methodology/">methodology</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="print:hidden"><PartnerOffers heading="Next: get real quotes" /></div>

    <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-6 text-sm leading-7 text-amber-950">
      <strong>About this estimate:</strong> this MVP uses a transparent planning model, not live mover quotes or a market-validated price database. Treat the result as a budgeting starting point and replace assumptions with real quotes.
    </div>

    <section class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6 sm:p-8 print:hidden" aria-labelledby="methodology-heading">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-700">How it works</p>
      <h2 id="methodology-heading" class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Transparent calculation methodology</h2>
      <div class="mt-5 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold">1. State distance</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Selecting two states fills the distance with a great-circle calculation between their centroids. This is a planning approximation rather than road mileage.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold">2. Known extra costs</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Travel, temporary housing, deposits/setup, and packing/extras are added exactly as you enter them. Unknown items remain at zero until you have an amount.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold">3. Planning buffer</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">A 10% contingency is added to the move and known extra costs. The displayed range is a planning band, not a confidence interval or provider quote.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-6 border-t border-slate-200 pt-5 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
        <p><strong class="text-slate-900">Source notes:</strong> the one-way truck-rental average by mileage band comes from <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href="https://www.uhaul.com/Tips/Loading/How-To-Save-Money-ON-Truck-Rentals-35820/" rel="noopener">U-Haul</a> (September 2025 data). It sets the minimum base for the move cost. A BLS labor-wage figure is stored for reference and does not change the result.</p>
        <p class="mt-3"><strong class="text-slate-900">Current model status:</strong> the DIY base is the larger of a simple distance model and the U-Haul average for the mileage band. Rental-truck and full-service types add a labor/service premium on top of that base, and that premium is still an explicit MVP assumption. Because the U-Haul figures are band averages, the estimate can step up when the distance crosses a band boundary (for example at 1,000 miles). U-Haul notes that one-way rates vary by origin, destination, truck size, move date, and inventory. Validate the result against route-specific provider quotes.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </section>

